.TH chgrp 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
chgrp \- change file group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chgrp
.I "group file ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chgrp
sets the group of each
.I file
to
.IR group ,
which is either a numeric gid or a name from
.BR /etc/group .
The owner is left alone.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  There is no
.BR \-R .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B chgrp
stops at the first file it cannot change and exits 1.  Files after that
one are not touched.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chown (1),
.BR chmod (1)
